KZ2 patch 6074: LD_VC_WAYS, set-associative slots for patch 2047's draw payload cache. Default 1
(off: patch 2047's direct-mapped placement, unchanged).

Root cause (an earlier change's split run kz2-r85-s3, [vtx-cache] deltas per 256 frames): in b-walk's heavy views the cache
misses 35-42 % of draws (light stretches 15-20 %), and 74 % of those misses are first sights ("seen" 95,512 of 128,573
misses at t=163 s; seen == evict exactly in every interval: every slot is occupied and every new key evicts one).
Patch 2047 maps a key to one of 16,384 slots and fills an entry only at the second sight of its key, so two keys that
share a slot and both come every frame evict each other every frame and are never filled, and a key that comes once
(per-frame geometry at a new ring offset) evicts a filled entry that then needs two more sights. Every such miss pays
the index read, remap, fetch and topology again (refs + remap + fetch ~104 ms/s in the heavy view).

Change: LD_VC_WAYS=N (1, 2, 4, 8, 16) groups the slots into sets of N ways. A key may sit in any way of its set; a new
key takes an empty way, else the least recently used one (a 64-bit access tick per entry). N = 1 is patch 2047's slot
exactly (set base = (h ^ h >> 32) & 16383). Only placement changes: a hit still needs the full key compare and every
source check of 2047 (tracked writes, page stamps, the full byte compare of LD_VTX_CACHE_FULL), so the payload a hit
replays is the same bytes as before; LD_VTX_CACHE=verify checks that live. New counter in the [vtx-cache] line (also
with N = 1): `evict-hot` = evictions of a filled entry used in this frame or the last one (the conflict misses that
ways remove), and `ways=N`. The set choice is in rsx_vc_ways.h (pure functions), tested by tools/runtime/test_vc_ways.sh
(with a negative control: the thrash and one-shot checks fail with one way).

Written for Project Pyrrhus (KZ2 runtime); no outside code.

